    "## EDA\n",
    "- `Train` has 95 articles (each article has two texts, 1 real 1 fake).\n",
    "- `Test` has 1068 articles.\n",
    "- Median length is 1373 and 1852 for real and fake texts.\n",
    "\n",
    "Since the median text lengths far exceed the `sequence_length` of typical models, hence will need account for significant truncation or use models that support longer sequences.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Missingness\n",
    "Articles 10 and 14 in the training set and article 223 in the test set have empty fake text files. I kept these rows, since empty text may appear during prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Special Characters\n",
    "There are special characters (☉, ি, േ, '്, ...) exclusively in fake train texts (22 out of 95) and never in real train texts suggests these characters are a strong indicator of fake content.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Article similarity\n",
    "Since the distributions of Jaccard similarity, TF-IDF cosine similarity, and semantic similarity are all right-skewed, it indicates that most article pairs have **low similarity scores**—meaning they share little vocabulary, word importance, or contextual meaning. This suggests that the pairs are largely unrelated to each other, rather than being paraphrases or closely matched texts."
   ]
