    "## Modelling\n",
    "\n",
    "There are several modeling options that are well-suited for pairwise text comparison tasks:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Transformer-Based Pairwise Models\n",
    "\n",
    "Fine-tuned Transformers (BERT, RoBERTa, DeBERTa):\n",
    "These models take both texts in a pair as input (formatted as [CLS] text_1 [SEP] text_2 [SEP]) and are highly effective at capturing deep semantic relationships, making them state-of-the-art for text-pair classification and ranking.\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentence Transformers:\n",
    "These generate embeddings for each text and enable direct comparison through similarity scoring, which is particularly valuable for semantic similarity and paraphrase detection.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Pairwise Ranking with Large Language Models\n",
    "\n",
    "Pairwise Ranking Prompting (PRP) with LLMs:\n",
    "Prompting large language models like Flan-UL2 or GPT-4 to choose between two texts has shown impressive results for preference alignment and ranking tasks, especially when fine-tuned or used with well-crafted prompts.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Siamese and Twin Network Architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "Siamese Networks:|\n",
    "These architectures encode each text with identical subnetworks and then compare their outputs, which is especially useful when the relationship between texts is more important than their independent classification."
   ]
