    "### Pairwise Ranking Prompting (PRP)\n",
    "This is a technique where you prompt a large language model (LLM) to compare two texts and decide which one better matches a given criterion (e.g., which is more \"real,\" more relevant, or preferred)\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "prompt = f\"\"\"Which of the following two passages is more real?\n",
    "\n",
    "Passage A:\n",
    "{text1}\n",
    "\n",
    "Passage B:\n",
    "{text2}\n",
    "\n",
    "Answer with \"Passage A\" or \"Passage B\" only.\"\"\"\n",
    "response = llm(prompt)[0]['generated_text']\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "To leverage the training data, we can consider the following techniques:\n",
    "1. **Fine-tuning**: futher train the LLM on the labelled training data and adjusts internal weights. Though we don't have aubstantial amount of labeled pairs (only 95).\n",
    "2. **RAG**: at inference time, retrieve relevant examples or facts from your training data and provide them as additional context to the LLM.\n",
    "3. **Prompt Engineering**: Include representative examples from your training data directly in the prompt (few-shot learning). For pairwise ranking, this means showing the model several example pairs and the correct choice before presenting the actual pair to be ranked."
   ]
